#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:31
msgid ""
"`randomize.isCrypto` will be `true` when a cryptographically secure "
"function is being used to generate random numbers. The value will be "
"`false` when the function in use is `Math.random`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:33
msgid "pattern"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:35
msgid "The pattern to use for randomizing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:37
msgid ""
"Patterns can contain any combination of the below characters, specified "
"in any order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:39 ../../source/randomatic_README.md:91
#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:104
msgid "**Example:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:41
msgid ""
"To generate a 10-character randomized string using all available "
"characters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:51
msgid "`a`: Lowercase alpha characters (`abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz'`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:52
msgid "`A`: Uppercase alpha characters (`ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ'`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:53
msgid "`0`: Numeric characters (`0123456789'`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:54
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`!`: Special characters (`~!@#$%^&()_+-={}[];\\',.`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:55
msgid "`*`: All characters (all of the above combined)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:56
msgid "`?`: Custom characters (pass a string of custom characters to the options)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:58
msgid "length"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:60
msgid "The length of the string to generate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:62
msgid "**Examples:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:64
msgid ""
"`randomize('A', 5)` will generate a 5-character, uppercase, alphabetical,"
" randomized string, e.g. `KDJWJ`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:65
msgid "`randomize('0', 2)` will generate a 2-digit random number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:66
msgid "`randomize('0', 3)` will generate a 3-digit random number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:67
msgid "`randomize('0', 12)` will generate a 12-digit random number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:68
msgid ""
"`randomize('A0', 16)` will generate a 16-character, alpha-numeric "
"randomized string"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:70
msgid ""
"If `length` is left undefined, the length of the pattern in the first "
"parameter will be used. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:72
msgid "`randomize('00')` will generate a 2-digit random number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:73
msgid "`randomize('000')` will generate a 3-digit random number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:74
msgid "`randomize('0000')` will generate a 4-digit random number..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:75
msgid ""
"`randomize('AAAAA')` will generate a 5-character, uppercase alphabetical "
"random string..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:77
msgid ""
"These are just examples, [see the tests](./test.js) for more use cases "
"and examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:79
msgid "options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:81
msgid "These are options that can be passed as the third argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:83
msgid "chars"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:85
msgid "Type: `String`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:87 ../../source/randomatic_README.md:100
msgid "Default: `undefined`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:89
msgid "Define a custom string to be randomized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:93
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`randomize('?', 20, {chars: 'jonschlinkert'})` will generate a "
"20-character randomized string from the letters contained in "
"`jonschlinkert`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:94
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`randomize('?', {chars: 'jonschlinkert'})` will generate a 13-character "
"randomized string from the letters contained in `jonschlinkert`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:96
msgid "exclude"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:98
msgid "Type: `String|Array`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:102
msgid ""
"Specify a string or array of characters can are excluded from the "
"possible characters used to generate the randomized string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:106
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`randomize('*', 20, { exclude: '0oOiIlL1' })` will generate a "
"20-character randomized string using all of possible characters except "
"for `0oOiIlL1`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:108
msgid "Usage Examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:110
msgid ""
"`randomize('A', 4)` (_whitespace insenstive_) would result in randomized "
"4-digit uppercase letters, like, `ZAKH`, `UJSL`... etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:111
msgid "`randomize('AAAA')` is equivelant to `randomize('A', 4)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:112
msgid ""
"`randomize('AAA0')` and `randomize('AA00')` and `randomize('A0A0')` are "
"equivelant to `randomize('A0', 4)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:113
msgid ""
"`randomize('aa')`: results in double-digit, randomized, lower-case "
"letters (`abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:114
msgid ""
"`randomize('AAA')`: results in triple-digit, randomized, upper-case "
"letters (`ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:115
msgid ""
"`randomize('0', 6)`: results in six-digit, randomized numbers "
"(`0123456789`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:116
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`randomize('!', 5)`: results in single-digit randomized, _valid_ non-"
"letter characters (`~!@#$%^&()_+-={}[]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:117
msgid ""
"`randomize('A!a0', 9)`: results in nine-digit, randomized characters (any"
" of the above)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/randomatic_README.md:119
msgid "_The order in which the characters are defined is insignificant._"
msgstr ""

